-- Taste Engine: initial Postgres schema (Supabase). Generated by drizzle-kit from
-- db/schema.ts; it replaces the five retired SQLite/D1 migrations and creates
-- their final state. Apply once to an empty database:
--   psql "$DATABASE_URL" -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 --single-transaction -f drizzle/0000_initial_postgres.sql
--
-- Storage conventions are unchanged from SQLite: 0/1 flags and counts are
-- integer, timestamps are ISO-8601 text, JSON is text. The only type change is
-- expires_at on refresh_locks, spotify_oauth_states and spotify_tokens, which
-- holds Date.now() milliseconds and so needs bigint (Postgres integer is 32-bit).
--
-- Why every table has ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY and no policy: Supabase exposes
-- the public schema through its REST API to anyone holding the public anon
-- key. With row level security on and no policies, that API can read and write
-- nothing. The server connects directly as the table owner, which row level
-- security does not restrict, so the application is unaffected.

